    <briefdescription>
<para>Concept satisfied by two integer types of different signedness. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The built-in comparison of a signed and an unsigned operand converts the signed one to the unsigned type, so <computeroutput>-1 &lt; 1u</computeroutput> is false. For these pairs the comparisons use the <computeroutput>std::cmp_*()</computeroutput> functions, which compare the mathematical values. <computeroutput>bool</computeroutput> and the character types are excluded, since <computeroutput>std::cmp_*()</computeroutput> do not accept them and their comparison with integers is not a sign problem. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
